    "EXECUTED READINGS (2026-10-14, quick-newt-81, one path each; rung = the MINIMUM across paths, DESIGN 4b.1). PATH 1, interpreted claims over LOCAL fixture mirrors FsList/FsNonEmpty (v2.test.claim.compiler.free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness): an empty variant at a nonempty-product return and formal refuses; structurally guaranteed for that shape. PATH 2, the BUILT native CLI (generation-one executable of gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli, `emit --entry` over the live dag root, real `import std.algebra { FreeSemigroup, Empty }`): `fn probe() -> FreeSemigroup<Int> { Empty }` is refused with arrow_body_does_not_inhabit_declared_return, located at the body: an observed refusal, not rung evidence; non-discriminating because the accepted control is unreachable and the same-type generic nullary case (fn f() -> FsList<Int> { FsEmpty }) also refuses. PATH 2 for the `[]` literal at a FreeSemigroup return or formal, and for the constructed positive control, is NOT ESTABLISHED: each refuses resolve_reason_unbound_symbol, and the closure's std.algebra, std.optional and std.unicode.types refuse resolve_reason_parameter_path_not_indexed, the #13832 regression (fn parameters not indexed under an alias type) that #13974 fixes; a refusal that is the same with the control is no reading of the wall. Root cause of why the in-memory fixture closure cannot evidence the literal: `[]` lowers to a reference to std.algebra FreeMonoid (v2.std.list_introduction list_introduction_head_path), and that closure holds only fixture modules; embedding std.algebra text there would be a second authority. compile_dag_diagnostic_census is NOT a route for this class: it is the v1 Rust host (its own doc says so), refuses the literal as InternalError, and emits unclassified rows for both the Empty RED and the control, so it cannot discriminate. Rung: structurally guaranteed only for PATH 1 shapes; the real-corpus FreeSemigroup `[]` seam is below that until #13974 lands and PATH 2 is re-run with the literal and the control. Next trigger: #13974 on main, then re-run the gen-one probe (four modules: `[]` at formal, `Empty` at return, `[]` at return, constructed control) and add the generic alias control.",

    "RUNG PER PATH (2026-10-14, gunbc#13910 landed; the class rung is the MINIMUM across in-scope paths, DESIGN 4b(1)). Three paths. (1) Interpreted v2 fixture path (v2.test.claim.compiler.free_semigroup_empty_producer_witness, local FsList/FsNonEmpty mirrors): an empty producer at a nonempty-product position refuses with a head mismatch from v2.std.inhabitance inhabitance_declaration_heads_differ, with accepted constructed, alias and generic positive controls: structurally guaranteed for the bounded nominal-head shape. (2) Built generation-one native CLI over the real std.algebra: UNESTABLISHED; the one Empty refusal is non-discriminating (see EXECUTED READINGS) and the `[]` literal and the accepted control are unreachable. (3) v1 seed merge path (the ONLY judge on the merge path today): silent -- the seed accepts the same source and nothing refuses, which is BELOW the ladder rather than mitigatable. Path 3 is an unclimbed path, not a rung drop: the seed never held a rung for this class, so gunbc.rung_drop declares nothing and the seed is not edited. The class therefore stands below mitigatable on the merge path, and its minimum below the ladder.",

    "POPULATION: UNMEASURED, NOT ZERO. Executed 2026-10-14 on the generation-one binary kept by `gunbc test //gunbc/instruments:v2-native-cli`, as `emit --entry <e> --source-root src/v2 --source-root dag`. Entry v2.cli.compile_cli: 209 closure members, 207 refused before inhabitance is reached (127 resolve_reason_parameter_path_not_indexed, 64 resolve_reason_unbound_symbol, 6 target_value_expr_reason_transform_shape_invalid, 5 produced_decl_type_ref_unrealized, 5 emit_module_member_*_not_realized or translate_module_not_a_type_expression), 2 accepted. Entry v2.compiler.compile: the whole closure refused, v2.std.integer requested by gunbc.witness.v2_native_route lies in a tree the requesting tree may not import. A zero count of head mismatches over those closures would be vacuous, so none is claimed: the native route cannot judge either closure of gunbc.emitted_subject_build_gate emitted_subject_build_rows. Re-measure when the parameter_path_not_indexed refusals clear (gunbc#13974 is expected to) and update this entry; any instance found is a live defect.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability: the native route resolves and judges the self-host and native-cli closures, and the native inhabitance check judges the required merge path -- the same capability as gunbc.rung_drop v2_native_route_off_the_merge_path, whose trigger this shares. Until then the seed route stays silent for this class.",
    "PROOF-CARRYING CONVERSION, BLOCKED ON A LANGUAGE CAPABILITY (2026-10-14, #13994 frontier; ruling nonemptiness_is_constructed_or_proved). A FreeMonoid proved nonempty reaches a FreeSemigroup position only through a named conversion nonempty_by_proof<T>(xs: FreeMonoid<T>) -> FreeSemigroup<T> whose call infer would judge (PLANNED, none of this exists yet: an expression-count fold over v2.std.cardinality CardinalityConstraint and cardinality_operation_laws; proved -> accepted, known-unproved -> refused, unknown count -> refused rather than undecidable-accepted, with typed reasons to be named when the judgment is built). The three seams and declared_type_inhabitance stay unchanged, because implicit admission on a proof is forbidden by DESIGN 4. The conversion cannot be declared today: a total body needs a value for its Empty arm and .dag has std.types Never but no generic Never eliminator and no refinement that makes the Empty arm unreachable (std.error_primitives pure_dag_seam_unreachable has projections for Int, Float and String only, and names the missing generic bottom as its own dissolve trigger); a self-call breaks bounded execution and a fabricated head is a DESIGN 5 fabricated default; no realization-binding mechanism exists for a bodiless pure fn. WHY std.types Never DOES NOT DISCHARGE IT TODAY (checked 2026-10-14): Never is the uninhabited TYPE, and an arm instantiated at it is unreachable by a binding's declaration (std.goal_assessment AssessRefusal). The Empty arm of FreeMonoid<T> is a NULLARY constructor of a fixed type, so there is no parameter to instantiate at Never; and the arm's obligation is to produce a FreeSemigroup<T>, which needs an eliminator Never -> T (none exists in std, std.types or the compiler) applied to a Never VALUE that the arm cannot obtain, because that would require narrowing xs by the count proof (a refinement of the scrutinee), which the checker does not carry. TRIGGER, two capabilities, no second bottom type: (1) an eliminator from std.types Never to every type, and (2) the checker narrowing a scrutinee by a proved cardinality so that the Empty arm is judged unreachable, i.e. holds a Never value; with both, nonempty_by_proof is an ordinary total body, and the Int/Float/String seam projections of std.error_primitives dissolve into the eliminator. Consumer of the cardinality carrier and count laws until then: none in production (declared frontier of DESIGN 3c); the judgment, its fold and its reason symbols are design, not authority.",
